/* ── The kpadopt4 secrets, time, cooking and commands in cyberpunk's own grammar [kpadopt4] ──
   A secret is decoded start to end in held steps (G2, G10); what runs out is a tripwire (G16); a thing that ends or
   fails is locked as a target in red (G13); a clock is a notched face with a held sector (a loop advances in whole ticks,
   G1); the wheel turns in ticks, never an ease (G1); a command is a prefixed label over a notched plate (G15). */
@layer kp.signature {
    /* ── Secret field ── */
    [data-theme='cyberpunk'] .kp-secret__value {
        border-radius: 0;
        clip-path: var(--kp-cp-clip-ctl);
