    /* ── Data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

    [data-theme='synthwave'] .kp-table {
        border-collapse: separate;
        border-spacing: 0;
    }

    /* One stripe across the whole header, not one per cell [gap-3, Kenny
       2026-09-10]. A `border-image` is painted per element by definition,
       so every `<th>` restarted the ramp and the seam he saw was the
       mechanism working exactly as written. The stripe now belongs to the
       row and runs the table's full width.

       `background-image` on the row rather than a border-image: a row is
       not a box that takes a border in every table layout, but it always
       has a background, and a 2px band pinned to its bottom edge is the
       same two pixels the border was. Measured across the register on
       2026-09-11: `.kp-table th` was the only place this declaration
       repeats side by side — the nav menu, form summary, card, theme menu,
       wizard and spec list carry it too and never sit in a row. */
    [data-theme='synthwave'] .kp-table th {
