       wallpaper and the words come up behind it (160 ms). Each close is that
       set played backwards, in the same time, by js/motion.js
       (`--kp-open: reverse-close`): the lacquer sinks, the inlay undraws to
       its start. The keyframes carry their easing per segment and name none
       of their own, so the reversed play is the mirror frame for frame.
       The dialog that is not yet open runs one and a half times as long, so
       the close js/motion.js reads off it (two thirds) is the opening's own
