    /* ── The keyboard cursor on a row is the film's ring [G5, mlp-r2-1018] ──
       js/row-select.js rings the cursor row (and the row that holds the
       focus while j / k walk). The base draws it as an outline in --ring,
       which in dark is plain ink: a white box round the row, the one ring
       on the page without the film (G5: "the film is every edge that
       matters, the line, the fill, the ring"), and on a table row the
       void channel of DI2's ring (a box-shadow) is not painted, so only
       the white line was left. Here the ring is the film itself, 2 px just
       inside the row, cut out of an --kp-iris plate with a mask, so the
       ticked row's light plate and the cursor's film read apart. It moves
       with the key at once: nothing fades or slides. An entity card keeps
       its own cursor (its ::after is the card's plate). */
    [data-theme='dark'] :is([data-kp-cursor-visible] .is-cursor, [data-kp-roving]:focus-visible):not(.kp-card) {
