    [data-theme='formal'] .kp-card__state > .kp-card__empty {
        padding-block-end: 1.25rem;
        border-block-start: 0;
        background: none;
    }

    [data-theme='formal'] .kp-empty__title {
        margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
        font-family: var(--theme-font-display);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
        font-style: italic;
    }

    [data-theme='formal'] .kp-empty__body {
        margin: 0;
    }

    [data-theme='formal'] a:not([class], :is(nav, [role='navigation'], [role='menu'], [role='menubar'], .kp-nav, .kp-sidenav, .kp-footer) a) {
        text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
        text-decoration-color: color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 55%, transparent);
        text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    }

    [data-theme='formal'] a:not([class], :is(nav, [role='navigation'], [role='menu'], [role='menubar'], .kp-nav, .kp-sidenav, .kp-footer) a):hover {
        text-decoration-style: double;
        text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
        text-decoration-color: currentColor;
    }

    /* Growing and shrinking, this theme's way [scope-142; approved by Kenny
       on research/size-motion, 2026-10-04]. js/motion.js marks a gliding box
       `[data-kp-resizing]` and what arrives in it `[data-kp-arriving]` (which
       is ruled in below, as every arrival is). The frame is ruled in as the
       box changes. */
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
        [data-theme='formal'] [data-kp-resizing] {
            outline: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
            outline-offset: 4px;
        }
    }

    /* ── Ruled open, ruled off [G1 to G4, G13; Kenny, 2026-10-08, questions 1
       to 4 and 13 of research/formal-character]. What opens is ruled open
       where it stands: its frame rule is ruled start to end at an even pace
       and stops dead at the margin (linear, 400 ms), the words revealed
       behind it; then each line under it is ruled the same way, top down,
       60 ms apart (a dialog's title, its sentence, its buttons; a menu's
       entries one by one; a drawer's head, body and foot; a tour card's
       title, text and foot); a 2 px navy pen runs ahead of the words and is
       lifted, from the start, 160 ms after it has reached the margin (the
       finished pose is bare). A close is the same motion played backwards,
       bottom first, end to start; what arrives is the leave turned around
       (`--kp-open: reverse-close`). Everything under prefers-reduced-motion:
       no-preference; standing still nothing is clipped and nothing is drawn.
       Mirrored by `dir` (`-rtl` keyframes, `--kp-fm-ltr`).

       Two machines, because js/motion.js plays a close and a leave two ways.
       (1) A dialog, a drawer, a tour card and what leaves or arrives are
       turned round by js/motion.js from the effects the browser reports,
       element by element and pseudo-element by pseudo-element. Said
       `--kp-lines: keep`, each keeps its own time and wait (its
       animation-delay) in the close, the open and the leave: one pair of
       keyframes per line (`kp-sig-formal-ruled-line`, the clip;
       `kp-sig-formal-ruled-pen`, the pen), the wait of the line as its delay
       (0, 60, 120 and 180 ms; a fourth line and later share the fourth's),
       over 740 ms (400 + 160 + three lines 60 ms apart). The shade behind it
       takes the whole time, as it does without the token. The unopened dialog runs 1.5
       times that: js/motion.js reads the theme's time from an unopened dialog
       and takes a close as two thirds of it, so a dialog opens and closes in
       exactly 740 ms, and `--kp-close-max` allows it. A leave is the
       arrival's reverse in 560 ms (400 + 160): the pen is set again, then the
       rule is taken off, end to start; the arrival is that played backwards
       by js/motion.js, and a toast comes in as it. (2) A menu, a popover, a
       tooltip and the other panels that hang from something are turned round
